{"_data": [{"contents": [{"type": "lesson_name", "content": ""}, {"type": "unit_name", "content": "Unified Modelling Language, UML: A Methodology? "}, {"type": "position", "content": 5}, {"type": "origin", "content": "stub"}, {"type": "lesson", "content": 1}, {"type": "level", "content": "A1.2"}], "type": "metadata"}, {"contents": [{"type": "test", "content": "false"}], "type": "achievment_test"}, {"contents": [{"type": "text", "content": "These are words you hear when talking about UML."}], "type": "target_word_describer"}, {"contents": [{"type": "primary", "content": "I can say what a methodology is related to information systems.   I can talk about UML as a diagramming notation.   I can list some diagrams used in UML"}, {"type": "secondary_1", "content": "Communicates effectively in English about the communicative topics for this level through the use of appropriate basic vocabulary and grammatical structures, and with intelligible pronunciation.  Exchanges simple information on programming tools and solutions to a client's requirement."}], "type": "objectives"}, {"type": "background_image", "content": "enpe8n2le01ob05re1img01.jpg"}, {"contents": [{"type": "heading", "content": "Demonstrative Pronouns in Negative Statements"}, {"type": "describer", "content": "You use  <span class=\"strong\">demonstrative pronouns</span> to replace nouns in a sentence or before nouns."}, {"type": "text", "content": "The <span class=\"strong\"> demonstratives pronouns </span>are: <span class=\"italic\"><span class=\"strong\"> This </span>, <span class=\"strong\"> That </span>, <span class=\"strong\"> These </span></span>and <span class=\"strong\"><span class=\"italic\"> Those</span></span>; you use them when you intend to point at a noun, or to replace a noun you mentioned before."}, {"type": "text", "content": "Use <span class=\"italic\"> <span class=\"strong\"> This </span> and <span class=\"italic\"> </span><span class=\"strong\"> These </span></span> to point at nearby things, and you use <span class=\"italic\"><span class=\"strong\"> That </span></span> and <span class=\"italic\"><span class=\"strong\"> Those </span> </span>to point at things that are far."}, {"type": "text", "content": "Examples:"}, {"type": "text", "content": "<span class=\"italic\"> <span class=\"strong\"> That </span>methodology works with any software. <br/>The company uses <span class=\"strong\"> this </span>diagram in UML.</span>"}, {"type": "text", "content": "You use <span class=\"strong\"> demonstrative pronouns </span> in negative statements with the present simple structure.  Remember, you add a <span class=\"strong\"> not </span>after the verb in present."}, {"type": "text", "content": "<span class=\"italic\"> <span class=\"strong\"> These are not </span>the correct diagrams. <br/> <span class=\"strong\"> This is not </span>working correctly. <br/> <span class=\"strong\"> Those </span>diagrams <span class=\"strong\"> don't </span>identify software requirements. </span>"}, {"type": "table", "content": "{\"rows\":3,\"columns\":3,\"cells\":[\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\" \\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"<span class=\\\"strong\\\"> Singular </span>\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"<span class=\\\"strong\\\"> Plural </span>\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"<span class=\\\"strong\\\"> Near </span>\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"This\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"These\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"<span class=\\\"strong\\\"> Far </span>\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"That\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"Those\\\"}\"],\"styles\":\" intro_table_border instruction_table_background\"}"}, {"type": "example", "content": "UML is not what you think, this is not a system of processes, this doesn't give us an outcome of the analysis, and this doesn't organize tasks sequentially"}, {"type": "example", "content": "UML uses diagrams because this is not a methodology, but a very precise diagramming notation."}, {"type": "example", "content": "Clearly, these are not barcodes, but they are diagrams that represent program designs and make them useful. \t"}, {"type": "example", "content": "UML is always popular for its diagramming notations, those are not textual notations, but they represent technical and graphical information."}], "type": "learning_points"}, {"contents": [{"type": "heading", "content": "Adverbs of Frequency: Sometimes"}, {"type": "describer", "content": "You use <span class=\"strong\"> adverbs of frequency </span>to express how often things happen."}, {"type": "text", "content": "<span class=\"italic\"><span class=\"strong\"> Sometimes </span></span>is an <span class=\"strong\"> adverb of frequency </span> that means something happens exactly half the time. In the following chart, you can see the adverb <span class=\"strong\"> sometimes </span>located exactly in the middle, as the adverb sometimes refers to thing happening at regular time intervals."}, {"type": "text", "content": "Normally, you place the adverb of frequency <span class=\"strong\"> before </span>the action verb. "}, {"type": "text", "content": "Example:"}, {"type": "text", "content": "<span class=\"italic\">They <span class=\"strong\">sometimes </span>apply the behavior diagram.</span>"}, {"type": "text", "content": "Remember that most of the time, when using sentences with verb to be, the adverb of frequency goes <span class=\"strong\">after </span>the verb."}, {"type": "text", "content": "Example:"}, {"type": "text", "content": "<span class=\"italic\">When the boss asks us to use diagrams in UML, he is <span class=\"strong\">sometimes </span>persistent on using another thing.</span>"}, {"type": "table", "content": "{\"rows\":2,\"columns\":7,\"cells\":[\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\" 100%\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"90%\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"70%\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"50%\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"30%\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"5%\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"0%\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"Always\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"Usually\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"Often\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"Sometimes\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"Occasionally\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"Hardly ever\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"Never\\\"}\"],\"styles\":\" intro_table_border instruction_table_background\"}"}, {"type": "example", "content": "People sometimes define UML as a methodology, but you have no idea of how mistaken they are."}, {"type": "example", "content": "It can be sometimes useful to organize an informational system, even when that is not what we look for in UML."}, {"type": "example", "content": "Diagrams, sometimes, use different arrows to indicate relationships, so those are not complicated because they usually have clear and understandable information."}], "type": "learning_points"}, {"contents": [{"type": "heading", "content": "Diagrams in UML"}, {"type": "describer", "content": "Diagrams are an incomplete representation of a system's model. "}, {"type": "text", "content": "You use <span class=\"strong\"> diagrams in UML </span> to identify software requirements, implementations, and behaviors. There are many types of d<span class=\"strong\"> iagrams in UML </span>depending on what you want to identify. For example, the ones that represent behavior can include aspects like interactions which you can organize in a hierarchical diagrams."}, {"type": "text", "content": "Remember, you can also use diagrams to detect omissions or errors in a system. These are the most common diagrams in UML: "}, {"type": "image", "content": "enpe8n2le01ob05img01.jpg"}], "type": "learning_points"}, {"contents": [{"type": "text", "content": "Look for more UML diagrams in your nearest library or on the Internet."}, {"type": "text", "content": "Make a list of structural UML diagrams and behavioral UML diagrams. "}, {"type": "text", "content": "Choose one structural and one behavioral diagram to explain in a short presentation, describing all their characteristics. "}, {"type": "text", "content": "Present it to your class and your teacher."}], "type": "takeaway_extension"}, {"contents": [{"type": "text", "content": "I search about UML diagrams."}, {"type": "text", "content": "I differentiate structural diagram and behavioral diagrams.  "}, {"type": "text", "content": "I explain a structural diagram and a behavioral diagram. "}, {"type": "text", "content": "I prepare a short presentation about structural and behavioral diagrams."}, {"type": "text", "content": "I present it to my classmates and teacher."}], "type": "takeaway_assessment"}, {"contents": [{"type": "name", "content": "UML "}, {"type": "definition", "content": "Unified Modeling Language"}, {"type": "part_speech", "content": "(abridging): "}, {"type": "example", "content": "Example: UML uses diagrams because this is not a methodology, but a very precise diagramming notation."}, {"type": "audio", "content": "enpe8n2le01ob05aud01"}], "type": "target_word"}, {"contents": [{"type": "name", "content": "diagramming notation"}, {"type": "definition", "content": "diagrams representing categories"}, {"type": "part_speech", "content": "(noun): "}, {"type": "example", "content": "Example: UML is always popular for its diagramming notations, those are not textual notations, but they represent technical and graphical information."}, {"type": "audio", "content": "enpe8n2le01ob05aud02"}], "type": "target_word"}, {"contents": [{"type": "name", "content": "methodology "}, {"type": "definition", "content": "system of processes you use to achieve a goal or requirement"}, {"type": "part_speech", "content": "(noun): "}, {"type": "example", "content": "Example: A methodology is the one that organizes activities within a sequence, and it can be sometimes useful to organize an informational system."}, {"type": "audio", "content": "enpe8n2le01ob05aud03"}], "type": "target_word"}, {"contents": [{"type": "name", "content": "outcome "}, {"type": "definition", "content": "result"}, {"type": "part_speech", "content": "(noun): "}, {"type": "example", "content": "Example: UML is not what you think, this is not a system of processes, this doesn't give us an outcome of the analysis, and this doesn't organize tasks sequentially."}, {"type": "audio", "content": "enpe8n2le01ob05aud04"}], "type": "target_word"}, {"contents": [{"type": "name", "content": "suppression "}, {"type": "definition", "content": "exclusion of clearly irrelevant information"}, {"type": "part_speech", "content": "(noun): "}, {"type": "example", "content": "Example: UML allows the suppression within diagrams, so authors can suppress any detail they consider not relevant."}, {"type": "audio", "content": "enpe8n2le01ob05aud05"}], "type": "target_word"}], "type": "sena", "labs": [{"exercises": [{"stimuli_ids": [0], "_data": [{"contents": [{"type": "Learning Outcomes", "content": "I can say what a methodology is to information systems. "}, {"type": "Learning Outcomes", "content": "I can talk about UML as a diagramming notation. "}, {"type": "Learning Outcomes", "content": "I can list some diagrams used in UML."}, {"type": "Free Header Item", "content": "What does methodology mean? Why is it important in information systems?"}, {"type": "Free Header Item", "content": "How does the diagramming notation work? Explain."}], "type": "instructions"}, {"contents": [{"type": "group_name", "content": "Welcome"}], "type": "