 [{"contents": [], "type": "instructions"}, {"contents": [{"type": "group_name", "content": "Quiz"}], "type": "group"}, {"type": "feedback", "content": {"attempt_feedback": [{"type": "text", "content": ""}, {"type": "text", "content": ""}], "correct_feedback": "Correct!", "incorrect_feedback": [{"type": "text", "content": "Whoops! Something important is missing."}, {"type": "text", "content": "Maybe next time..."}], "allowed_attempts": 2}}, {"contents": [{"type": "skill", "content": "Reading"}], "type": "learning_skills"}], "id": 10}, {"stimuli_ids": [], "template_override": 1, "questions": [{"_data": [{"contents": [{"type": "pdf", "content": "enpe8n2le01ob05re7pdf01.pdf"}], "type": "question"}], "responses": [{"_data": [{"type": "text", "content": ""}], "selected": 0, "correct": 1, "id": 0}], "id": 0}], "type": "DWS", "_data": [{"contents": [{"type": "text", "content": "Structural Diagram and Behavioral Diagrams "}], "type": "instructions"}, {"contents": [{"type": "group_name", "content": "Take Away"}], "type": "group"}, {"type": "feedback", "content": {"attempt_feedback": [{"type": "text", "content": ""}, {"type": "text", "content": ""}], "correct_feedback": "Correct!", "incorrect_feedback": [{"type": "text", "content": "Whoops! Something important is missing."}, {"type": "text", "content": "Maybe next time..."}], "allowed_attempts": 2}}, {"contents": [{"type": "skill", "content": "Reading"}, {"type": "skill", "content": "Writing"}, {"type": "skill", "content": "Speaking"}], "type": "learning_skills"}, {"contents": [{"type": "text", "content": "Instructions: Complete the following steps. Fill in the Self-Assessment."}], "type": "post_instructions"}], "id": 11}], "stimuli": [{"_data": [], "id": 0, "contents": [{}], "type": "welcome", "template_override": 1}, {"template_override": 1, "contents": [{"value": {"audiosrc": "enpe8n2le01ob05re2aud01", "images": [{"time": "100", "image": "enpe8n2le01ob05re2img01.jpg", "id": 0, "text": "<div align=\"justify\"><span class=\"strong\">Specialist: </span>People sometimes define UML as a methodology, but you have no idea of how mistaken they are. UML is not what you think, this is not a system of processes, this doesn't give us an outcome of the analysis, and this doesn't organize tasks sequentially; in other words, this is not a methodology itself. A methodology is the one that organizes activities within a sequence, and it can be sometimes useful to organize an information system, even when that is not what we look for in UML.</div>"}, {"time": "38000", "image": "enpe8n2le01ob05re2img02.jpg", "id": 1, "text": "<div align=\"justify\">On the other hand, UML is always popular for its diagramming notations, those are not textual notations, but they represent technical and graphical information. Clearly, these are not barcodes, but they are diagrams that represent program designs and make them useful. Diagrams, sometimes, use different arrows to indicate relationships, so those are not complicated because they usually have clear and understandable information.</div>"}, {"time": "69000", "image": "enpe8n2le01ob05re2img03.jpg", "id": 2, "text": "<div align=\"justify\">Diagrams don't need to follow a standard methodology or process because these are not mandatory requirements for creating designs. Remember that they don't express precise graphical notations. UML uses diagrams because this is not a methodology, but a very precise diagramming notation. Every single diagram is useful for three or more applications within the system; for instance, you can use object diagrams for describing the data within the system or package and class diagrams for describing the architecture of the system. UML usually uses different arrows for precisely giving meaning to each notation. <br/>Finally, UML allows the suppression within diagrams, so authors can suppress any detail they consider not relevant. Those details always include essential information for the reader.</div>"}], "coverimg": "enpe8n2le01ob05re2img01.jpg"}, "type": "slideshow"}], "type": "audio", "_data": [], "id": 1, "title": ""}], "id": 0, "_data": [{"contents": [{"type": "has_nav", "content": true}, {"type": "has_exercise_controls", "content": true}], "type": "lab_options"}], "type": "scholar"}]}